o pull a trigger  a nearby army officer pointed out that  murdering a member of the American  Military In Cold Blood was a capital  offense in other words if glass shot  Fitzgerald he'd be hanged immediately  it must have taken a huge amount of  willpower to lower his weapon remember  what he'd come through to get to this  point but lower it he did however he  left Fitzgerald with a passing promise  if he ever left the protection of the  army glass would find him and he would  kill him  because he had a very particular set of  skills skills he'd acquired over a very  long career  glass would live on the American  frontier for the rest of his life  trapping trading hunting and exploring  he was a veteran of many battles of the  various tribes whose lands the United  States of America was slowly claiming  for its own  but it was in 1833 at the approximate  age of 50 that his luck finally ran out  he and two fellow Trappers were ambushed  by a large party of arakara Braves  whilst crossing a frozen River they were  all shot robbed and finally sculpt  in the years since Hugh glass's  remarkable story has quite rightly  achieved legendary status  but as with many legendary Tales there's  a fairly good chance that some of it  isn't true much of what we know about  glass's life comes from sources that are  hard to trust entirely and Rumor Has It  Glass himself was fond of telling Tall  Tales particularly when they concerned  himself  exactly where we should draw that line  between fact and Fable is Up For Debate  but one thing's for certain even if on  the attempt of the story is told about  Hugh glass are true he was undeniably  one of the most remarkable men and  greatest survivors ever to have lived  foreign
 

